# Credentials & secrets
.credentials.json

# Honeypot harvest dirs — must never be tracked. Substring match so
# `quarantine`, `quarantine-old`, `container-staging/.../quarantine`,
# etc. are all covered.
**/*quarantine*

# Ephemeral state
history.jsonl
mcp-needs-auth-cache.json
dates/state.json
last-statusline.json

# Plugin runtime data
plugins/

# Homunculus runtime state (observer archives, PIDs, per-project memory)
# Skill content lives in ~/Repos/everything-claude-code/.claude/homunculus
homunculus/

# Scratch/tmp folder
tmp/

# Dev-container staging tree, written by the claude-cl-sync systemd unit.
# That unit declares three ReadWritePaths under ~/.claude — homunculus/,
# container-staging/ and dev-container/.venv/ — and only two of them had a
# rule. This one stayed invisible purely by luck: everything staged so far
# happens to be named `homunculus/` or `*quarantine*`, which other rules
# catch. The first differently-named artefact would have dirtied the tree.
container-staging/

# Step-back detector runtime state (per-session flags + classifier log)
step-back/

# Runtime/cache directories
cache/
debug/
downloads/
backups/
file-history/
session-env/
shell-snapshots/
telemetry/
paste-cache/
sessions/
powerline/usage/today.json
powerline/usage/pricing.json

# Project-specific data (per-project, not global)
projects/

# Tasks & plans (session-specific) — anchored to root so dev-container/plans/ tracks
/tasks/
/plans/
**/__pycache__/

# Caveman state flag
.caveman-active

# Dev-container user-local overrides
dev-container/proxy-allow.txt

# Powerline / per-session usage telemetry
usage-data/

# Cron-driven log output. All runtime-emitted logs are ignored;
# hand-curated ones (review-agent.log) are negated back in.
logs/*.log
!logs/review-agent.log

# Externally cloned skill repos (each has its own .git; track upstream
# as submodules later if pinning becomes useful)
skills/caveman/
skills/planning-with-files/

# Python virtualenvs + build artefacts inside tools/
**/.venv/
tools/*/state.json

# Token-optimizer runtime (plugin data dir + backups)
token-optimizer/
_backups/

# Homunculus observer artefact
observer-last-run.log

# Claude Code session lockfile
.settings.lock

# Worker runtime state (scaffolded by CC on each run)
workers/.claude-profile/backups/
workers/.claude-profile/projects/
workers/.claude-profile/sessions/
workers/.claude-profile/.claude.json
workers/*/scratch/

# Local-only permissions (CC writes dynamically)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Credential backups (.credentials.json itself already ignored above; .bak-* variants too)
.credentials.json.bak-*

# Timestamped backups tooling drops next to the file it rewrites
# (settings.json.bak-*, mission.md.bak-*). Ephemeral by construction, and
# nothing ever cleans them up — so left untracked they made every autosync
# run report a dirty worktree forever.
*.bak-*

# Background-worker daemon runtime: supervisor log, per-job scratch, and
# daemon/control.key — a live credential that must never be auto-committed.
daemon.log
daemon/
jobs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Claude Code harness state files — the complete registry, not a sample
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# These are written by the `claude` binary itself into its config home, so
# there is no writer of ours to relocate: gitignore is the only lever. The
# list below is not guesswork and not "what happened to show up in git
# status" — it is the harness's own state-name registry, read out of the
# ELF at ~/.local/share/claude/versions/2.1.251:
#
#   L = new Map([["daemon-status","daemon.status.json"],
#                ["active-time-ledger","active-time.json"], ...])
#
# Every id in that map resolves to a file directly in ~/.claude. Ignoring
# only the ones currently on disk is how we got here: `daemon.log` and
# `daemon/` were ignored while `daemon.status.json`, `daemon-auth-status.json`
# and `daemon-auth-cooldown` — same subsystem, same directory — were not, and
# they dirtied the checkout the moment a background worker ran and the login
# expired. Enumerate the registry once so the NEXT one is covered before it
# appears.
#
# Two registry entries are DELIBERATELY absent: `keybindings.json` and
# `CLAUDE.md` are real user config that belongs in this repo.
active-time.json
daemon-auth-cooldown
daemon-auth-status.json
daemon.json
daemon.scheduled.status.json
daemon.status.json
.deep-link-register-failed
gh-pr-status-cache.json
hfi-auth.json
loop.md
.npm-cache-cleanup
policy-limits.json
remote-settings-consent.json
remote-settings-helper-consent
remote-settings.json
server-sessions.json
.session-log-cleanup
stats-cache.json
.version-cleanup

# Session-reflection hook output: per-session stdout/stderr logs, skipped-
# recursion records, idle-handoff logs and counters. Pure runtime — 1496 files
# of it were auto-committed once, and handoff.log mutates on every session, so
# left tracked it turns each autosync run into a churn commit.
reflections/

# Repo-autosync runtime state (per-repo cache, security alerts, logs)
repo-autosync-data/

# Ralph-loop state, one file per armed session id. Pure per-session runtime;
# the gate scripts live in hooks/ + scripts/ and are tracked.
ralph-loop/

# Scheduled-task lockfile (ephemeral)
scheduled_tasks.lock

# Cleanup timestamp (runtime)
.last-cleanup

# Auto-updater outcome stamp (runtime)
.last-update-result.json

# Home-manager-managed skill symlinks (point into /nix/store)
skills/nixos-config-dev
skills/nixos-vm-test-gate
skills/nixos-agent-testing
skills/nixos-automated-testing
skills/nixos-agenix-secret

# CI-stability monitoring runtime (per-PR logs + state)
loops/

# Prompt-log JSONL (populated by hooks/prompt-log.py) — high-churn,
# session-local. Skill /prompt-review-weekly clusters into backlog.
automation-review/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bulk data / pre-redaction artefacts — never commit
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything below is pattern-based on purpose: the goal is to block the
# NEXT file of this shape, not just the one that prompted the rule. Once
# bulk or unscrubbed data is pushed, removing it needs a history rewrite.
#
# Live backups now sit outside the repo entirely:
#   ~/.local/share/claude-transcript-backups/

# Pre-redaction / pre-migration copies. `.orig` also catches merge-conflict
# leftovers; `.pre-*` catches any "snapshot before I mutate this" file.
*.orig
*.pre-scrub
*.pre-*
!.pre-commit-config.yaml

# Backup directories of any name (transcript-backups/, foo-backups/, ...)
*-backups/
*.backup

# SQLite caches/DBs. These are runtime state or bulk corpora, never source.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# JSONL is the house format for transcripts, observation logs, harvested
# datasets and label files — all runtime or bulk, none of it source. No
# .jsonl file has ever been tracked here. If one genuinely belongs in the
# repo, add it deliberately: git add -f <path>
*.jsonl
*.jsonl.gz
*.ndjson

# Compressed archives — nothing in a config repo should ship as a tarball.
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.zip

# Runtime lockfiles are per-run state. Generalises the one-off .settings.lock
# and scheduled_tasks.lock entries above. Dependency lockfiles are genuine
# source and negated back in — flake.lock is already tracked under
# skills/visual-verify/.
*.lock
!flake.lock
!Cargo.lock
!poetry.lock
!uv.lock
!Gemfile.lock

# Auto-sync runtime log (see sync-agent.sh)
sync.log

# runtime log, rewritten each run (repo-autosync, 2026-08-16)
logs/review-agent.log

# experiment run output (transcripts, final outputs, state) (repo-autosync, 2026-08-17)
experiments/*/runs/
experiments/*/runs-pilot-discarded/

# Tombstone. self-compact's runtime state (UUID session dirs + logs) moved to
# ~/.local/state/claude-self-compact/ on 2026-08-20, so nothing should write
# here any more. Kept anyway: the old ~/.claude/self-compact/ tree survives on
# disk until the migration is verified, and repo-autosync auto-commits whatever
# is untracked in this repo — an unignored leftover gets committed, not merely
# shown in git status. Now anchored to the repo root, which the unanchored form
# was not: it also matched skills/self-compact/, so every file added to that
# skill after 2026-08-18 would have been silently ignored (SKILL.md survived
# only because it was already tracked).
/self-compact/

# Working notes symlink -> ~/.local/state/claude-tasks/ (userspace, never committed)
tasks
